#adm/daemons/mailmesg.c
remain ({"elon@eastern stories",})
mesg "BEGIN FORWARDED TEXT:Elon writes:> Title: error reporting and a role-play environment> From:  Digitizer> Date:  Thu Mar  9> > Imagine it: you're Redblood Battlehammer, a dwarf with an attitude.> You waltz up to the local bar to have a few beers, listen to some> gossip, and maybe pick up on some information about that black army> that's been spotted travelling from the castle.  Suddenly, a sneaky> fellow behind you makes a quick movement, and a small knife lands> in the wall just beside your head.  You turn to confront the little> vermin, and...> > Your sensitive mind notices a wrongness in the fabric of space.> > *sigh* Don'cha just hate it when that happens?> > What I'm looking for are ideas on how to report the fact that the game> has suffered from an error _without_ breaking the whole feel of the> role-play situation.  When I first started playing LPs, that sensitive> mind garbage told me nothing: I thought it was part of the game, and> that I was being watched or something.> > I would rather not report errors at all to players, and simply mail> or leave a bug notice with the coder responsible.  However, the> player needs to know that they're not responsible for something> not working.> > So, I'm looking for suggestions based on what the rest of you use> on your particular muds, if you happen to do something other than> the sensitive mind messaging, or the \"You have encountered an> error...contact an admin.\" messages.> > Digitizer> > > "
